.TH EDUKA-CUSTOMIZER 1 "October 2026" "Eduka-Customizer 0.12 Alpha" "Edukasaun OS"
.SH NAME
eduka-customizer \- ISO builder and customizer for Edukasaun OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eduka-customizer
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPROJECT\fR] [\fB\-D\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B eduka-customizer-pkexec
[\fIPROJECT\fR|\fIISO\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Eduka-Customizer builds Edukasaun OS live images from Debian stable, testing
or sid. A project holds the root filesystem (\fIrootfs/\fR), the ISO tree
(\fIiso/\fR), boot images (\fIboot/\fR), caches, logs and the built images
(\fIoutput/\fR). Ubuntu and Ubuntu-based images are refused.
.PP
Without a command the graphical interface starts. Most commands need
administrator rights.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui [PROJECT|ISO]
Start the graphical interface.
.TP
.B new [PATH] \-\-iso FILE | \-\-bootstrap SUITE | \-\-snapshot dist|backup
Create a project from a Debian or Edukasaun OS live ISO, a new Debian base
(mmdebstrap) or a copy of the running system.
.TP
.B info
Show the project, the detected system and the last ISO.
.TP
.B shell [COMMAND...]
Open an interactive root shell inside the image.
.TP
.B run COMMAND...
Run one command inside the image.
.TP
.B hook [SCRIPT...]
Run hook scripts inside the image (default: \fIPROJECT/hooks/*\fR).
.TP
.B sources \-\-suite stable|testing|sid [\-\-backports] [\-\-deb\-src] [\-\-mirror URL]
Write a clean deb822 \fI/etc/apt/sources.list.d/debian.sources\fR.
\fB\-\-add\fR \fINAME\fR \fB\-\-uri\fR \fIURI\fR \fB\-\-suites\fR \fIS\fR [\fB\-\-key\fR \fIURL|FILE\fR]
adds a third-party repository.
.TP
.B apt install|remove|upgrade|update|deb|list|search|file ...
Manage Debian packages inside the image.
.TP
.B flatpak setup|install|remove|list|search [APP-ID...] [\-\-firstboot]
Flathub applications, installed into the image or on first boot.
.TP
.B desktop catalog|install|session|dm|list|session-type|compositor|sddm-theme [NAME] [\-\-type x11|wayland] [\-\-preset P]
Desktop environments, window managers, sessions, login screens, X11/Wayland and compositors.
.TP
.B eduka-desktop [\-\-repo URL|DIR] [\-\-ref REF] [\-\-deb FILE] [\-\-set SECTION.KEY=VALUE]
Fetch, build and install Eduka-Desktop and set its defaults for new users.
.TP
.B brand identity|plymouth|plymouth-generate|wallpaper|login|locale VALUES...
Identity (os-release), Plymouth themes, wallpaper, login screen and locale.
.TP
.B branding apply|generate|build|key|show [\-\-logo F] [\-\-wallpaper F] [\-\-keyring \-\-email E]
Build and install the <id>-branding package (identity of base-files, lsb-release,
distro-info-data, desktop-base, Debian logos, GRUB, Calamares) and optionally
<id>-archive-keyring. The editable source lives in PROJECT/branding/.
.TP
.B workshop open|build|restore|list [PACKAGE] [\-\-no\-hold]
Copy an installed package to PROJECT/workshop/PACKAGE for direct editing,
rebuild and install it (held by default), or restore Debian's version.
.TP
.B themes list|apply|packs|import [ITEMS...] [\-\-gtk T] [\-\-icons T] [\-\-cursor T] [\-\-font F] [\-\-dark]
Default look for all desktops, theme packs and theme import.
.TP
.B language list|show|set [LOCALE] [\-\-extra L...] [\-\-timezone TZ] [\-\-keyboard K] [\-\-variant V] [\-\-no\-packs] [\-\-boot\-menu L...|all] [\-\-no\-calamares]
Default language, keyboard, time zone, translations, the Language submenu of
the ISO boot menu and the Calamares defaults.
.TP
.B calamares show|install|set MODULE KEY=VALUE...|branding|slides FILES|users|partition|live\-password [PASSWORD]
Edit the Calamares installer. Values are YAML, e.g.
.B calamares users min_length=8 autologin=false
or
.B calamares set welcome requirements="{requiredStorage: 15}".
.TP
.B plymouth list|install SOURCE...|apply NAME|remove NAME|packages [PKG...]|preview NAME [\-\-apply] [\-\-seconds N]
Plymouth themes from .deb, .zip, .tar.*, folders or Debian packages.
.TP
.B kernel list|available|install PKG...|third\-party backports|liquorix|xanmod|xanmod\-lts|deb FILES|remove VERSION|iso VERSION|initramfs|firmware|grub KEY=VALUE... [\-\-headers]
Kernels of the image and the GRUB defaults of the installed system.
.TP
.B bootmenu list|show FILE|edit FILE [\-\-from F] [\-\-once]|revert FILE|apply
Edit GRUB, ISOLINUX and EFI image boot files (e.g. efi.img:EFI/boot/grub.cfg);
.B apply
rebuilds the ISO in seconds without recompressing the system.
.TP
.B live [\-\-session S] [\-\-resolution WxH] [\-\-mode skel|root|sandbox]
Run the image's desktop in a nested Xephyr window; changes are saved into the image.
.TP
.B build [\-\-compression zstd|xz|gzip|lz4|lzo] [\-\-boot\-mode auto|replay|generate] ...
Build the hybrid BIOS/UEFI ISO image.
.TP
.B test [\-\-firmware uefi|bios|secureboot] [\-\-disk]
Boot the image in QEMU.
.TP
.B recipe apply|export [FILE]
Apply or export a JSON recipe (reproducible builds).
.TP
.B clean [\-\-unmount\-only] [\-\-all]
Unmount everything and remove caches (or the whole tree).
.TP
.B doctor [\-\-fix]
Check (and install) the host tools.
.TP
.B download [\-\-suite stable|testing] [\-\-list] [FILE]
Download and verify an official Debian live image.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/eduka-customizer/eduka-customizer.conf
Global settings (Debian codenames, mirrors, Eduka-Desktop repository, build defaults).
.TP
.I /usr/share/eduka-customizer/exclude.list
Paths excluded from the squashfs.
.TP
.I PROJECT/project.json
Project state and history.
.TP
.I /tmp/eduka-customizer/
Developer logs: eduka-customizer.log, errors.log and bug reports.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo eduka-customizer new ~/eduka --iso debian-live-13.1.0-amd64-lxqt.iso
sudo eduka-customizer -p ~/eduka desktop install eduka
sudo eduka-customizer -p ~/eduka flatpak install org.kde.gcompris \-\-firstboot
sudo eduka-customizer -p ~/eduka build
eduka-customizer -p ~/eduka test \-\-firmware uefi
.fi
